s": 5.247, "runIndex": 1, "textCheck": {"status": "PASS", "alphanumericCount": 818, "distinctWords": 79, "taskTerms": true, "flags": [], "method": "the runner's generated text (parsers: textExtraction) + lexical screen; full text retained"}, "textOutputSHA256": "e74d901523779e6ea107fa971a0476fe41cf93518cf3d53c19bfd7d5fa6ac33a"}, "metrics": {"promptTokenCount": 1338, "generatedTokenCount": 255, "promptTokensPerSecond": 1344.7236180904522, "decodeTokensPerSecond": 66.64924202822792, "firstTokenLatencyMS": 995, "loadTimeSeconds": 0.233, "coldRun": true, "harnessStamp": "executorch-mac-v1-2026-10-08", "initialThermalState": "nominal", "finalThermalState": "nominal", "memoryPeakResidentMB": 1204.875}, "harnessStamp": "executorch-mac-v1-2026-10-08", "decodedText": "<think>\nOkay, the user wants me to list 25 distinct things on-device AI that a phone can do a cloud model can't. Each item should have two full sentences of explanation. Let me start by understanding the query.\n\nFirst, I need to list 25 things. On-device AI refers to AI models that run on a device like a phone, not on a cloud. So, the tasks a phone can do that a cloud can't. Maybe things like camera, voice assistants, etc.\n\nI should start by listing some common things that phones do. Then, think of things that cloud AI can't do. For example, camera for phone, voice assistant for phone, etc. Then, make sure each item has two sentences. Let me check if I have 25 items. Let me think: camera, camera, voice assistant, voice assistant, etc. Then, explain each with two sentences.\n\nWait, the user provided a passage with 17 items. But the query is about listing 25 things. So, maybe the 25 items are similar to the 17 items but more varied. Let me think of 25 things. Maybe include things like camera, voice assistant, etc., and also include things like cloud", "outputSample": "<think>\nOkay, the user wants me to list 25 distinct things on-device AI that a phone can do a cloud model can't. Each item should have two full sentences of explanation. Let me start by understanding ", "provenance": {"definitions": "prefill tok/s = prompt_tokens / (prompt_eval_end_ms - inference_start_ms) * 1000. The window opens before the runner tokenizes the prompt (TextLLMRunner::generate sets inference_start_ms, then encodes), so prefill includes tokenization.\nTTFT ms = first_token_ms - inference_start_ms = the same window (first_token_ms is taken when prefill returns, before the first token is decoded to text).\ndecode tok/s = generated_tokens / (inference_end_ms - prompt_eval_end_ms) * 1000, generated_tokens = tokens of the decode loop; the reply has one more token, the one prefill sampled.\ncold = one generation in a fresh llama_main process (no --warmup). warm = llama_main --warmup: one unmeasured generation of the same prompt and max_new_tokens in the same process, stats and KV position reset, the second generation measured.\nClock: integer milliseconds (extension/llm/runner/util.h time_in_ms).", "recipe": "Qwen3-0.6B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048.recipe.json", "recipeSha256": "0ad0c744008d58f8d3707eb73f813481e71b8052c67cf756466402becd49994f", "recipeAlias": "et1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-g128-emb8", "exporter": "extension/llm/export/export_llm (examples/models/qwen3/config/qwen3_xnnpack_q8da4w.yaml)", "modelProvenance": "own export with the ExecuTorch tag's own exporter (recipe.json beside the .pte); not a published artifact", "promptFile": "Qwen3-0.6B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048.prompts/long-context-1024-gen256.chat.txt", "promptSha256": "360771899cd15f27bcedd5911f5c7f6775ccc15a092e2d133ec29cd83c90baf2", "tokenizer": "tokenizer.json", "tokenizerSha256": "aeb13307a71acd8fe81861d94ad54ab689df773318809eed3cbe794b4492dae4", "textExtraction": "stdout minus the echoed prompt, cut before '\\nPyTorchObserver '", "statsLine": "PyTorchObserver {\"prefill_token_per_sec\":1344.72,\"decode_token_per_sec\":66.6492,\"prompt_tokens\":1338,\"generated_tokens\":255,\"model_load_start_ms\":1791399435709,